  "query_preview": "..Main concerns this week will be heat and return of\nmoisture. \n\nHeat: High pressure aloft will be strengthening across the area\nthis week bringing the hottest temperatures so far this year.\nTuesday thru Thursday will be the hottest days with some locals\nnear record highs, especially east of Tucson. HeatRisk in major\ncategory across eastern Pinal, eastern Pima, Gila River Valley \nand upper San Pedro Valley (north of Benson). With that said, \nwent ahead and issued Excessive Heat Watch for the above areas \nfor Tuesday and Wednesday. Will see on Monday if time and areal \ncoverage needs to be expanded into Thursday.\n\nMoisture: Dry thru Tuesday. Will start to see some moisture\ninflux from the south mid-week on for a low end 10-30% chance \nof afternoon and evening thunderstorms Wed-Fri mainly SE of \nTucson.\n\nNext weekend: Well above normal high temperatures continue with\nslight chance of afternoon storms across far SE Cochise county.",
